S = sup_s sum_{j<=26} |g_j| 3^j = 12578.828890
   (g_j are G_2's coefficients; they decay like R^-j, R<5,
    so the head captures nearly all of S)
C = S/6 = 2096.471482   [in |R_k| <= C (k+3)^3 3^-k]
K0 from S = 57

C_2 = max_i |h_i''| 3^i / i^2 = 10.8165
C = C_2/18 = 0.600919   [in |R_k| <= C (k+3)^3 3^-k]
K0 = 33

NOTE: C_2 here is a max over i <= NMAX.  Extending it to all i needs
a tail argument -- the Cauchy bound on the pole-free part supplies
one, and is only needed for i > NMAX where it is far less lossy.
